;;; A rule's `:assert (not ?g)` with `?g` its parameter, which the activator `(deny Bob)` binds to a name —
;;; M1f **W84**, register row `W84/not-name-parameter`, filed by S1f.7.4 (T1f.7.4.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; Two guests, of whom Ann has paid, and a rule `deny` whose parameter is what it
;;; negates, with the activator `(deny Bob)`. No candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The activator binds `?g` to `Bob`, a name, which the program shows: refused at
;;; load, one line, on every command. With the activator `(deny (paid Bob))` the rule
;;; stores `(not (paid Bob))`.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `55aadd0b`, release: the program loads and the rule stores `(not Bob :rule deny)`;
;;; R is {∅}, exit 0 on every command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.4 (T1f.7.4.3).

(relation paid Guest :why "{?1} has paid")
(is-a Ann Guest) (is-a Bob Guest)
(paid Ann)
(deny Bob)
(rule deny (?g) :match () :assert (not ?g) :why "not {?g}")
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (paid ?g))
